// V3 negative fixture (plans/backlog/FORMAL_VERIFICATION.md task 8).
//
// The CALLER-side obligation: `recip_bugged` calls the contracted
// `safe_div` without establishing `y != 0` — the callee's `requires`
// must be PROVED at the call site under the caller's path condition,
// and nothing constrains d, so it REFUTES with d = 0. Note the file is
// deliberately MIXED: `safe_div` itself verifies fine (its own ensures
// proves under its own requires); only the caller fails — modular
// verification means one bad caller does not poison the callee. The
// correct twin is `recip_ok` in tests/spec/verify_straight_line.test.yo
// (requires(d > 0), discharges the callee requires, proves).
pragma(Pragma.Verify);

safe_div :: (fn(x : i32, y : i32, requires(y != i32(0)), ensures(r == (x / y))) -> (r : i32))(
  x / y
);

recip_bugged :: (fn(d : i32) -> (r : i32))(safe_div(i32(1), d));
